nemesis@pcuf.fi (Ville Salo) writes:

>And everybody is going to be honest? I doubt it...and besides, some players
>think it's more demanding to play LOW scores instead of billions. I'd rather
>swap bones-files. How about that?

I made a suggestion like that one or perhaps two years ago, and I really
like the idea. Basically use XRD (external data representaion) for the
bone files and text for the score files. Destribute via News (r.g.h.data?)
Only send new top scores (or perhaps amoung the top ten) from a site, so as
not to clobber the net with those quick deaths.
Now how do we avoid those save & restore scores?
Suggestion, mark each character with a unique number which goes in the high
score list, that way each character will only get entered once, not each
time it dies. This will not mean that 'cheating' will be impossible but the
sites doing this exchange will mostly be sites with a security system and the
chance that anybody can do a save & restore is less likly then PC's.
Perhaps a nice feature would be to let the player go into explore mode when
he/she dies (this could allso be the action to take when restoring a
character which is allready on the high score list)

